+# Agent Note: Community Windows installer and account usage
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-13-community-windows-installer.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The community distribution needs installation without a separately installed Node.js or pnpm, plus visible request estimates and account balance. The previous portable distribution suffered shared extraction cleanup and a crashing Windows directory dialog.
+
+## Decision
+
+Keep the official desktop host, offline seed, transaction manager, and single-instance lifecycle at upstream commit fb2c4b9e698e30edb738bca4cf0618587db7d203. A separate community electron-builder configuration produces a per-user one-click NSIS installer with the bundled Node.js and pnpm. It has its own identity and default data directory, no official update feed, and no claimed official signature.
+
+Compose the existing browse directory picker in the desktop profile. Hide Node-spawned command windows without changing restricted-token CreateProcess flags. Packaging accepts either a JavaScript or executable pnpm entry.
+
+The LLM remote reads the saved provider account through its adapter. Only the official DeepSeek origin is accepted; redirects and raw error bodies are not exposed. The client queries on demand. Missing or failed balances are unavailable, never zero.
+
+Turn accounting optionally retains original attempts and launch timestamps. The chat estimates CNY with the September 12, 2026 price snapshot, original model, cache buckets, and peak window. Unsupported or incomplete accounting has no price. Estimates are not invoice deductions.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Continuing the old temporary portable shell leaves extraction lifetime coupled to runtime files. Replacing the entire official UI increases maintenance scope. Inferring each request charge from account balance differences misattributes concurrent account activity. Reusing the official updater can overwrite community features.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The source changes preserve the upstream runtime composition while adding a small billing surface. Distribution updates are manual. A packaged-runtime smoke test installs offline with a fresh DSH_HOME and no Node on PATH, boots the real host, loads HTML, and checks a second launch. Windows 10 hardware, real paid requests, and a live user's account balance remain separate acceptance checks.
